    "patchSets": [
        {
            "number": 1,
            "revision": "3e083c31edddddff1a076fae782a94529eb341c6",
            "parents": [
                "cb8d100b2f740ac8b2b382586786a8148fbc43fc"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/03/91803/1",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Ramya Sivakumar",
                "email": "sramya@ami.com",
                "username": "sramyagit"
            },
            "createdOn": 1782712228,
            "author": {
                "name": "Ramya Sivakumar",
                "email": "sramya@ami.com",
                "username": "sramyagit"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Palaniappan Arunachalam",
                        "email": "palaniappana@ami.com",
                        "username": "Palaniappanarunachalam"
                    },
                    "message": "LGTM"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "The main concern I have with this is we're changing the existing behavior. Before, if one of these calls failed, we'd get an unhandled exception and crash the service. Then we'd try a few restarts of the service and Quiesce the BMC if it continued to fail. Now we'll just log an error to the journal and continue. That seems like undefined behavior. What if we log the error but still just throw the exception?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ramya Sivakumar",
                        "email": "sramya@ami.com",
                        "username": "sramyagit"
                    },
                    "message": "I agree the current try/catch changes the failure semantics. \n\nIf the goal is only to improve observability, the safer pattern is to log the exception and then rethrow it. That preserves the existing fail-fast behavior while still adding context to the journal. I\u2019d recommend changing these handlers to catch (...) {log; throw;}\n\nlogging and then throw; is the correct approach"
                }
            ],
